La The mare's reproductive season or heat lasts 21 and 23 days and they are irregular, since it consists of two cycles. There are 14 days known as the anestrus cycle during which the female is not in heat and therefore does not accept the male but it is the preparation period for the embryo to develop, and the estrous cycle when the female is actually in heat, and goes into ovulation that usually lasts two days.
On the other hand, the horse is attracted to the female since she releases pheromones that are present in the urine. It also begins a kind of courtship towards the female.
4 Signs that a mare is not in heat
Be careful, it is not the same oestrus that menstrual cycle, typical of the human being. The oestrus It manifests itself depending on the season of the year, temperature characteristics, diet, the presence of male odors, age and lactation.
The mare is one of the animals listed as seasonal polyesters. This group includes all those living beings whose females have long photoperiod estrous cycles (times when it gets dark later and the daylight hours are longer).
The first estrus usually occurs at 15-24 months, depending on the breed, and arises from spring to fall.
The mare is in heat when the male is sexually receptive. This can be detected by observing whether the female displays a number of behaviors or signs:
Repeatedly raises the tail to show the vulva. This act may not occur if the male around him is quite aggressive.
They roll back the lips of the vulva to expose the clitoris.
Not all of the mentioned signs happen, as not all mares are the same. It can also happen, something that is very normal, that there is not a stallion with which to stimulate her at that very moment and thus decipher if she is in heat or not.
There is also the possibility that our mare is from passive type, which means that it does not present a positive or negative behavior towards the male. These mares, on occasions, allow them to be covered by the horse without being in heat.
Signs that a mare is not in heat Contrary to what happens in the heat period, when our mare is no longer located within it, her behavior as a general rule is: aggressive to the male's attempts to mount, does not tilt the pelvis nor does it separate the hindquarters, does not lift the tail and it can even reach bite and kick to the stallion.
One of the unmistakable signs that a male horse is in heat are his relinchos, which become much more continuous, prolonged and in a much higher and energetic tone.
As a curiosity, the horse's penis can reach one and a half meters in erection, which favors the excitement of the mare in just seconds.
It is necessary to have a series of previous knowledge, especially in relation to the state of heat in the horse. Gaining special relevance in the case of females.
