Horse carriages are carriages made up of a large box which can have various shapes and that is on two or four wheels. Carriages were used since ancient times to transport goods or people.
Currently, they are used mostly at events or special occasions, as in certain parties or weddings, its use is also frequent for tourist purposes or, those of more value, can be seen turned into museum pieces.
Their use became so widespread that it reached a point where they had to be banned in certain areas, their uses were restricted or prohibitions were made on certain types of carriages drawn by a certain number of horses. They were vetoed for some specific personalities; certain types of materials were established or prohibited in the decoration of the carriage itself, etc.
In 1578, Felipe II prohibited having horse carriages unless they were to be pulled by four horses that belonged to the owner of the carriage.
Carlos II in 1678, prohibited the use of buggies and other carriages, in addition to prohibiting the use of mules and males.
Road car, was that intended for longer trips due to its more comfortable design for travelers.
Running board car, is the one with seats in the doors.
