When they are still foals, some experts can observe their potential based on the shape of their legs, how they walk, their general morphology and their intelligence. When equines are one year old, their training begins.
Let's talk a bit about their morphological characteristics, although taking into account that they can have many variations from one specimen of the breed to another. They have a long and slender body, straight profile, with a very strong kidney that provides great power in the gallop.
The character is something that distinguishes this equine breed and it is that they are usually very intelligent, nervous, energetic and very sensitive horses. This makes it necessary to have a special hand when raising and training them.
Between the years 1683 and 1728, in England, breeders began to cross English mares with three Arabian stallion horses imported from the Middle East and with good distance racing skills: Darley Arabian, Byerley Turk and Godolphin Arabian. All modern Thoroughbred Horses descend from one of these three stallions, whose first part of the name refers to their owners and the second part to the breed to which the animal belonged.
