History of the most expensive horse in the world
In the first place, his name already gave his figure a certain power, and that is because he was baptized that way due to the death in 2009 of Bobby frankel, the one who was one of the best horse trainers of recent times and whose life was taken away by an unfortunate and macabre disease such as leukemia.
As soon as he was born, Frankel made certain all the hypotheses and assumptions generated about his figure. A foal with a powerful physique, supernatural energy and devilish character had just arrived in the world.
Perhaps, the more the irruption of someone in a certain context is expected, that starting gun may be a failure, although with time this misstep will be solved. However, with good old Frankel, it was not like that, quite the opposite.
The good winning streak continued over time to the point that he made the condition of undefeated his greatest virtue. Of course, it should be noted that all these triumphs took place in competitions that did not exceed a mile.
Unsurprisingly, Frankel had the power to take on more demanding competitions and he did. In the same way that he won in short races, He did it in longer-distance races and in iconic settings like New York.
As time passed, Frankel was gaining value not only as a runner, but also as a possible stallion. This led his owner to decide to withdraw him from competitions and give him a new role.
This is roughly the story of one of the most famous and expensive non-human athletes on the planet. According to many, seeing him on the track was comparable to seeing Maradona himself play or Muhammad Ali boxing.
