Horses and humans have been together for a long time, so long that we have been able to see a thousand times how amazing these animals are. Their strength, their elegance and their intelligence have made them indispensable companions for many people, who did not hesitate to pay tribute to them whenever they could.
At, Horses parade with their riders that, as in the past, continue to be sold, and throughout the week, only for the day, there is a great parade of horse carriages that circulate through the central streets. In addition, various activities related to the world of the horse are practiced, such as the hitching, morphological and driver contests whose prize for the winner is the Golden Horse.
To be able to enjoy it to the fullest You have to be there a week after the Seville April Fair and before the Rocío Pilgrimage. During those days, Jérez de la Frontera opens the door of the González Hontoria Park to welcome seven or nine days (depending on whether the previous weekend is incorporated) to joy, entertainment, and above all to the beauty of the horse.
The first thing to know is that we will find more than 250 booths, each with its own settings and gastronomic specialties, where in all probability they will serve us an oloroso or fine wine. The first, typical of the Marco de Jerez and Montilla-Moriles, is dark gold in color and aromatic; the second instead is a dry white wine made from palomino grapes that can be combined with lime sodas.
Of course, everyone can wear the suit with which they feel most comfortable, but in a traditional Fair like this one, it is very well seen that the women wear the flamenco dress and the men a short dress, which consists of a »wide-brimmed» hat or cowboy gorilla, a white shirt, white trousers, a short jacket in shades of gray or navy, and high-top jeans, or a half-seam suit.
In addition, Do you know that design contests are held?
The Horse Fair is, therefore, an opportunity to demonstrate the creativity of the participants, but also to show the world that is an excellent candidate to be declared as Intangible Cultural Heritage of Spain, something that by the way, has already been proposed.
Horses require strict customs and practically exact routines, unlike humans who tend to complain when the days are the same, in the case of horses, if they could express their wishes in words, they could ask us to always be the same, leaving of course a separate issue that has to do with balance, between rest, training and feeding time for each of the horses.
The more calm horses are, the happier they are and tranquility should not be understood as doing nothing, since in many cases the jobs enjoy training, this can be seen in many stables, but it should also be taken into account that rest and the hours grazing are vital, especially if they can share with others in their herd.
