La Centered Riding It is a respectful and creative method that helps the rider to better communicate with his horse through increased body awareness.
Centered Riding is about teaching from an initiation level to an Olympic level, to enjoy a gentle and respectful riding between rider and horse. This teaching method mixes the exercises and thoughts of methods such as Alexander Technique and at martial arts such as Tai Chi and Quigong, to increase balance and coordination of the mind and body.
Horses are proven to react to our stresses and the force that we apply and our imbalances, tensions and lack of rectitude can cause a blockage of communication between horse and rider. For this reason, Centered Riding teaches us what our own anatomy is like and helps us discover how we function in motion, opening up new possibilities in riding.
This technique is called chiropractic and treats the biomechanical dysfunction suffered by the horse's spine composed of muscles, nerves, ligaments and bones. All of them are those that protect the spinal cord and therefore those in charge of safeguarding all internal organs.
These types of internal injuries are caused by the equine has taken wrong steps that make you lose coordination, at the same time, that injure other joints and tendons or ligaments of the extremities. We will notice that he has pain or injury because the horse will change his posture to compensate for the restricted mobility of his spine to avoid pain.
