the name "Lusitano" comes from the word "Lusitania", a Roman region located west of the Iberian Peninsula, place linked to the origin of this equine breed. This region corresponds to Portugal, hence the Lusitanian horse is also commonly called "Portuguese horse."
The arrival of the English Thoroughbred made it lose fame during the XNUMXth century, but its characteristics and character made it finally regain its popularity.
