3 How do you remove ticks from a horse?
How do they bite?
As soon as they find the right place, they pierce the skin with their "teeth" called chelicerae and begin to suck blood. As soon as they start, they secrete a kind of cement around the mouthparts in order to obtain a good anchorage while feeding.
The first thing to be clear about is that we cannot take them with our fingers and pull them, because the only thing we will achieve is that the head remains inside and expels fluids, which may contain viruses or bacteria. It is very necessary to use tick remover tweezers that they sell in any pet store.
What to do if you have a lot?
When the horse has many ticks, what you have to do is treat it with a specific antiparasitic for these animals that, again, the veterinarian can recommend. However, If we want to try natural remedies first, we can do the following:
Cook many stems of pennyroyal (more or less, the ones that will fit in one hand). The remaining infusion is put into a sprayer and sprayed on the animal.
Although it is not usually fatal, it is necessary to be examined by a veterinarian and given the appropriate treatment so you can recover. Now, we have to bear in mind that there is no definitive cure: the horse will carry the disease for the rest of its life.
