3 How long does it take to tame a horse?
To gain the trust of a horse we actually have to act the same way we would if we wanted to befriend any other domestic animal, only much bigger and stronger . This means that you have to observe their movements and their gaze to know how far it will allow us to go.
The halter is an accessory that will be very useful for working with our horse. But before you even put it on, we must get him to get used to our hands, putting them near his head, ears and neck.
It is also important that we rub his snout with it. After a few days, we will put it on without fastening and we will see his reaction: if it looks calm, perfect, we will take it off and the next day we will fasten it; But if he looks nervous, we'll take it off him and spend some more time getting used to it.
Finally, we will have to put the pieces of the ears, without adjusting the straps.
With the branch, we can start teaching you some orders such as »tall», »standing», »walking» and »back». But also, the horse must respect our space.
We will leave it for a few minutes and then we will remove it. We will do this several times over the course of a few days so that little by little it becomes familiar to you.
You've got it? If so, now is the time to get him used to the stirrups while working with the branch line.
