The horse is normally larger than the dog in constitution, but it is often the case that it can be frightened of the dog since, by nature, the horse is an animal of escape and the dog is a predator. This is not to say that these two animals cannot get along and even make a great team.
The first thing our dog should learn and the human teaching is to respect places like the stables, dogs are very prone to sneaking. You can get close to them, but never cross them and, if you do, you will have to scold him with a resounding "no".
It is normal that when the faces are seen for the first time, the dog tends to bark, which will make the horse try to run away and will even become so nervous that it will raise its legs and kick with the danger that it poses for people around his side. In this case, we must strengthen our dominance status over the dog with a tug on the leash followed by a firm "don't bark."
