3 How many kilos of food do I have to give him?
Therefore, it cannot catch prey, so it becomes possible prey. What's more, their jaws are made to chew grass, but it is not a ruminant like the musk ox, but it can also eat flowers and fruits.
It has an approximate capacity of 15 liters and a very acidic pH: between 1.5 and 2, essential to be able to absorb the protein from the grass. Passing this vital organ, we find the small intestine, which is divided into the duodenum, jejunum and ileum, and has a length of about 21-25m.
400 different species of microorganisms inhabit here that are responsible for absorbing fiber from the food that the horse ingests. The whole process, that is, from when the food enters the mouth until it is expelled through the rectum it may take between 22 hours and 2 days, depending on the quality you have and the amount you have ingested.
So that you have good health it is very important to respect the instinct of each animal. In the case of the horse, being a herbivore it would not make any sense to give it, for example, meat since, in addition to being a waste of time and money, its body would not know how to digest it correctly.
A horse will need to eat several times a day, but it must be borne in mind that its stomach is small and we cannot give it large quantities. It will always be better to give a maximum of 1,8kg in 3 or 4 feedings., than to give him 3 or 4kg in one go.
