La equinoterapiaAlso known as hippotherapy or equestrian assisted therapy, it is a way of helping people who have special needs or who, for whatever reason, have withdrawn into themselves and have trouble communicating.
The benefits are many and varied. TO psychological and cognitive level, are these:
A communication and language level, these:
People with autism are people with a psychological disorder characterized by the concentration they put on their own inner world, thus losing contact with external reality. For them, doing therapy with horses is a way to regain (or gain) self-esteem and autonomy, thus reducing social anxiety.
People with Down Syndrome are people who suffer from a genetic disorder that prevents them from relating normally. They are very prone to depression, mania, and psychotic disorders.
A therapy horse has to be submissive, calm and docile. It is also very important that you show confidence in the rider, so he should treat his animal with respect, patience and affection, always using positive training.
