Following this, users have started complaining about another issue, and this time it is a serious one. Instagram is blocking the content of users claiming that the content doesn’t meet the community guidelines.
Here is all we know so far.
It may be blocked partially or fully depending on the content you have uploaded. This feature exists on almost all social media platforms including, Instagram, TikTok and Facebook.
If you are publishing a post on TikTok and Instagram and the number of likes and suddenly decline, you can assume that the video is being shadowbanned. The application will reduce the reach of your future posts as well.
“When IG knows you tryna promote something they immediately shadowban you. They’re so weird like,” said another user.
If you are being shadowbanned on the app, you might have breached any of the community guidelines. Follow the below tips to get rid of the shadowban.
You may have to remove all the TikTok videos and promotional content from the platform.
You may also need to take a break from posting content. Try to upload content that doesn’t contain logos of any other platform or company.
Avoid liking, messaging too much because Instagram might consider it a bot activity and it will block you permanently from the platform.
Avoid sharing explicit content and links on the platforms.
Sharing abusive content and hate speech is also prohibited on the platform.
Publishing so many posts in a short time span may also create trouble for you.
Read all the guidelines of Instagram and try not to breach any of them in order to avoid being shadowbanned from the platform.
