If your posts aren’t getting enough views and engagements on TikTok, you might have been shadowbanned from the app, but what actually is the meaning of Shadowban?
Besides getting banned, TikTok users sometimes face difficulty in reaching a higher audience, the post reach declines and so do the engagements. This may cause because the user has violated any of the community guidelines or because a large audience has reported the profile.
In case of breaching any of the community guidelines, video creators may face a shadowban on the app. After getting shadowbanned from the app, the content creators might feel difficult to reach a higher number of audiences.
So if you don’t want to face a shadowban on the video-sharing app, you must bear the following points in your mind.
Removing a bulk of videos from your profile may give a negative impression to the TikTok admin. They may think that you are trying to get away by removing the content that isn’t approved according to the community guidelines.
Using copyrighted content is illegal by law, doing so may suppress your views.
