If you are live on TikTok then you might have heard people asking How To Get Unshadowbanned On TikTok. Are you wondering to know what the term shadowbanned’ actually means?
TikTok is a Chinese application that enables the users to share videos only (unlike other social media applications). People from all age groups use this platform as it contains amazing content for all of them.
If your videos on TikTok are barely getting any view then there is a possibility that your account has been shadowbanned’. Let’s discuss in more detail that How To Get Unshadowbanned On TikTok.
The content will be partially or fully blocked. Also know that this type of banning will not stop you from uploading any of your new videos rather it will simply disable the content to reach the Foryou page of TikTok or to reach your followers.
Luckily, shadowbans last for few days only. The general consensus is that a first-time shadowban may be in effect for up to 14 days, but it might take longer if you have got shadowbanned more than one time.
Here’s how to get rid of this temporary ban on TikTok,
After removing the Cache and the videos that were against TikTok’s terms and conditions, now delete the application from your device and then reinstall it later. Login to your account again and look if the account has become normal or not.
