Has TikTok ever told you that your video is under review?
We are here for help. Here is all you must know about what does a video under review means on the video-sharing app.
Imagine you have spent hours recording a video, a couple of more minutes to edit the video, and when finally the video is all set to rock the screens, TikTok asks you to wait because the video is under review. Well, this is something really disappointing.
The meaning of Video Under Review is, your video cannot go live until it is being reviewed for any restricted content. Sometimes it takes few hours for the video to be reviewed while in some cases it may even take more than a day.
Most of the time the videos are being reviewed by bots and it takes few hours for the whole process. While in some cases, the video takes more than a day to be reviewed because your video has to be checked by a human to decide whether or not the video is appropriate for the platform.
Hence, the community guidelines are there to prevent inappropriate content to join the platform. This is the reason why most of the TikTok videos go under a strict review process before being able to publish on the site.
Make sure that your videos aren’t explicit in nature and they do not feature any violence. Furthermore, also make sure that you aren’t copying any already existing content or it may not fall under the copyright infringement category.
