However, some nations observe it on 11th November every year. The day of Remembrance is also known as Poppy day because Poppy is the symbol that presents this day.
Poppy was sparked as an inspiration for people by a Canadian officer named John McCrae. He dedicated it as the representation of people who lost their lives.
When asked about when to wear poppies, they are commonly worn from the start of the Great British Legion’s Poppy Appeal till Remembrance Sunday. For this year, the poppy appeal began on October 28th, and Remembrance Day will be observed on November 14th.
If you observe deeply, you will witness Queen wearing poppies on her left side. However, Royal British Legion has revealed that there is not a correct or incorrect way to wear poppies.
What does each color represent? Well, red and white poppies are worn to pay tribute to people who lost their lives while purple poppies are worn to pay respect to the animals that passed away because of the war.
This was all about what Remembrance Day is and why people wear poppies on this particular day. Hopefully, you have got all the information you needed to know.
