In a recent report published by Forbes, Google’s Chrome privacy settings are at stake and the application might be involved in nefarious purposes. This report by Forbes has gone viral on the internet and users are left concerned.
Here is the solution.
How To Check Chrome Settings?
As the users are looking to get rid of this application, a Google spokesperson has come forward to address the concerns. The spokesperson of Google said, “We intentionally limit the resolution of motion sensors in Chrome, and since 2019 we’ve had controls that allow users to block websites from accessing a device’s motion sensors altogether.
However, users do not seem impressed by the clarifications given by Google. Thus, they are searching for how to remove Google chrome from their devices.
Getting rid of Chrome from your device is quite simple for Apple users but Android users might face trouble as it is the built-in browser in most android devices.
On your device, long tap on the chrome app.
Open your phone and head towards the settings option.
Tap on the three dots located on the right hand corner.
Tap on ‘Motion Sensors’ and disable the option.
