The new TikTok feature enables you to add captions to your videos, but how to access this feature on the Chinese video-sharing app?
To lead the list of most popular social media applications, all the social media giants are continuously working on adding new features to the platform. Every single is thriving to enhance the user experience in order to retain their old followers and also to attract new users.
One of its recent updates helps the users add Add Caption On TikTok Videos, here we have provided how this feature can be accessed and used to create more engaging videos. Have a look!
Here is how you can add captions manually on the TikTok videos.
To generate auto captions on your videos initially launch your updated TikTok app and click on the “+” icon.
Once you have finished recording or uploading the video, tap on the check button that is located in the bottom right corner.
After writing the caption, you can change the font style, color and alignment.
This is how you can add and edit the TikTok video captions manually.
To enable the auto caption option for your TikTok videos follow the below steps.
Once you are done recording, tap on the red checkmark to hop into the editing corner.
Then you will be directed towards a button that reads, “Turn on Auto Captions”. Check this button to turn the auto captions feature on.
Here it is important to note that, you cannot edit the captions once the video is published. So, check the captions vigilantly before you hit the publish button.
