Which is better, naturalization or marriage?Timing of naturalization application
⇒ This page supports multiple languages; you can click the upper right corner to select your language
If you are thinking of marrying a Japanese person and are also thinking of applying for naturalizationIsWhich should be done first, marriage or naturalization, I think you may get lost.From the conclusion, it cannot be said unconditionally which is better.Both Understand the advantages and disadvantages Then, it is a good idea to make a choice that suits your wishes.The following is an easy-to-understand explanation by an administrative scrivener.
If you are thinking of marrying a Japanese person and are also considering applying for naturalization, you may be wondering whether you should marry or naturalize first, or apply for naturalization first. I think.
On the other hand, if naturalization is permitted and you marry a Japanese person after acquiring Japanese nationality, you can get married in the same procedure as a marriage between Japanese people, so the marriage procedure is easy.
So, in general, I will explain what kind of situation should be taken and the timing of naturalization and marriage.
This is because there is a provision of the Nationality Law that if the father or mother who has a legal parent-child relationship at the time of birth of the child is a Japanese national, the child will acquire Japanese nationality at the time of birth.So, for example, a child born between a Japanese husband and his spouse, a foreign mother, acquires Japanese nationality.
In this case, if you apply for naturalization while you are single, you will not be permitted due to residence requirements. If you have not lived in Japan for more than 5 years and have no work experience (other than part-time job) with a status of residence (visa) that allows you to work for more than 3 years, it depends on the time of marriage.
・ Persons who do not have a working status of residence (working visa) This is also for the same reason as the above "people who have not lived in Japan for more than 5 years", and although it depends on the time of marriage with the Japanese, the benefits of applying for naturalization from the standpoint of a Japanese spouse Will be big.In the first place, you cannot apply for naturalization immediately unless you marry a Japanese person.
2-2 Disadvantages of applying for naturalization after getting married first
As mentioned above, the marriage in this case is an international marriage.
・ Although it is not essential, for example, if you are staying in Japan for a family stay or study abroad, you may not be able to continue to stay with your current status of residence. You need to apply for immigration.
This is because when you apply for naturalization as a Japanese spouse, you will need to prepare additional documents such as a copy of the family register of the Japanese spouse, resident's card, and income-related materials.
Four.Renewal of period of stay is required even after applying for naturalization
Here, I explained the advantages and disadvantages based on the general idea.But most importantly, what is the best for you who are looking to apply for naturalization.Which should be done first, naturalization application or marriageIf you have any concerns, please contact the administrative scrivener corporation Climb..
